Experiment 5(b)
Title: Write a shell script that takes filenames as command line arguments & converts all of them to uppercase.  

Steps to follow:
Open the terminal in Ubuntu.  
Create a shell script: nano upper.sh  
Enter the following code:
#!/bin/bash
for file in "$@"
do
    mv "$file" "$(echo "$file" | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')"
done
```[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span)


Save the file using Ctrl + O, press Enter, then Ctrl + X.  
Give execute permission: chmod +x upper.sh  
Create some sample files: touch apple.txt banana.txt  
Execute the script by passing file names as command line arguments:
./upper.sh apple.txt banana.txt  
Check the result: ls 
The file should now appear as: APPLE.TXT and BANANA.TXT  



Result:
Successfully created and executed a shell script that converts the given file names to uppercase.  
